# for an explanation of the syntax see "man clone-exclude"
#
# For clarity, put your entries here (above the default entries below), e.g.
#-/home/<user>/Music/*

# According to the Filesystem Hierarchy Standard (FHS) the following directories
# contain data that is temporary and used while a system is running and may 
# change after a reboot. Therefore, they don't need to be cloned and are
# excluded. It's best not to modify them unless you really know what you are
# doing.
-/dev/*
-/proc/*
-/run/*
-/sys/*
-/tmp/*
-/media/*
-/mnt/*
-/var/cache/*
-/var/lock/*
-/var/run/*
-/var/tmp/*
